  q(REAS,'A pulse oximeter reading jumps around when the patient moves. What is the likely cause?','Motion artifact',['Low battery only','Wrong date set','Overly bright screen'],'A','Use motion-tolerant sensors or a different site, such as the earlobe.',MET),
  q(REAS,'A blood pressure cuff gives falsely low readings. Which cause is most likely?','Cuff too large for the arm',['Cuff too small for the arm','Arm below heart level','Patient talking during reading'],'B','A cuff that is too large reads falsely low, while a cuff that is too small reads falsely high.',MET),
  q(REAS,'An infusion pump shows an “air in line” alarm. What should be checked?','Air in the IV tubing',['The patient’s pulse rate','The pump’s serial number','The room’s Wi-Fi signal'],'C','Prime the tubing properly, remove bubbles and check for loose connections before restarting.',MET),
  q(REAS,'A defibrillator battery fails a capacity test. What is the best action?','Replace the battery and retest',['Charge it once and ignore','Remove the battery and use AC only','Mark it passed if it turns on'],'D','Batteries must meet capacity specs so the device works when needed.',MET),
  q(REAS,'Several devices on one circuit stop working at the same time. What should be checked first?','The circuit breaker',['Each device’s software','The patient’s chart','The device manuals'],'A','A tripped breaker can cut power to every device on the circuit.',MET),
  q(REAS,'A suction unit runs but produces weak suction. Which cause is most likely?','A leaking lid or tube',['The power cord is too long','The room lights are too bright','The unit is too clean'],'B','Check seals, canister lids and tubing for leaks and blockages, then test vacuum level.',MET),
  q(REAS,'A thermometer reads 2 °F too high against a reference. What should be done?','Calibrate or remove it from service',['Use it as is for all patients','Subtract 2 °F in your head','Tape over the display'],'D','Devices out of tolerance must be calibrated or repaired before use.',MET),
  q(REAS,'What is the first step in any troubleshooting process?','Gather information first',['Order a new device right away','Open the case and replace boards','Ask the patient to fix it'],'A','Ask the user what happened, try to reproduce the problem and check simple causes.',MET),
  q(REAS,'A ventilator shows a high-pressure alarm. Which cause should be suspected?','A kinked or blocked tube',['A disconnected circuit','A large leak in the cuff','An empty oxygen tank'],'B','High pressure suggests obstruction; low pressure suggests a leak or disconnect.',MET),
  q(REAS,'A device repeatedly blows its fuse. What should the technician suspect?','An internal short circuit',['A fuse rated too high for it','A clean power cord','A new battery'],'C','Find and repair the short before replacing the fuse again with one of the same rating.',MET),
  q(REAS,'Which tool is used to test a defibrillator’s energy output?','Defib analyzer',['Oscilloscope probe','Pressure gauge','Light meter'],'D','Analyzers measure delivered energy into a 50-Ω test load that simulates a patient.',MET),
  q(IT,'Which network address uniquely identifies a device’s network interface hardware?','MAC address',['IP subnet mask','Domain name','Port number'],'A','IP addresses can change, but MAC addresses are tied to the hardware.',AAMI),
  q(IT,'Why should default passwords on medical devices be changed?','To block unauthorized access',['To speed up the device','To change its screen colors','To save electricity'],'B','Default passwords are widely known and are a common attack route.',AAMI),
  q(IT,'Which type of software attack locks files until a ransom is paid?','Ransomware',['Spyware','Adware','Firmware'],'C','Hospitals have had to divert patients during ransomware attacks.',AAMI),
  q(IT,'What is firmware?','Software built into hardware',['A type of network cable','A fire safety code rule','A cleaning solution'],'D','Firmware updates must be validated before installing on medical devices.',AAMI),
  q(IT,'Which network device directs traffic between different networks?','Router',['Monitor','Keyboard','Printer'],'A','Routers and firewalls help keep medical device networks separate.',AAMI),
  q(IT,'What does a firewall do?','Filters network traffic',['Cools the server room air','Stores patient images','Prints device reports'],'B','Firewalls block unauthorized traffic to and from medical devices.',AAMI),
  q(IT,'Which wireless standard is commonly used for patient monitors and infusion pumps?','Wi-Fi',['AM radio','Analog fax','Infrared'],'C','Wireless medical devices need strong encryption and reliable coverage throughout the unit.',AAMI)
